# The V-Pot of strip 1 of an X-Touch in MC mode on the channel's pan, as
# the MCU reference describes the messages: CC 16 a relative turn, note
# 32 the push, note 73 ALT, CC 48 the ring, 0x10 its mode from the centre out plus
# LED 1 to 11, 6 the centre.

# Five detents clockwise; the ring follows at once, and the first frame
# shows the others centred.
> b0 10 05
! set /channels/ch1/pan/lr 0.1
< b0 30 17, b0 37 16
+ 25
# Two anticlockwise, bit 6 set.
> b0 10 42
! set /channels/ch1/pan/lr 0.06
# A push alone does nothing; with ALT held it centres the pan.
+ 25
> 90 20 7f
> 90 20 00
! none
> 90 49 7f
> 90 20 7f
! set /channels/ch1/pan/lr 0
< b0 30 16
> 90 20 00
> 90 49 00
! none
# The ring follows the pan another session writes.
@ {"changes": [{"path": "/channels/ch2/pan/lr", "value": -1}]}
< b0 31 11
# Banked by a channel, ring 1 shows channel 2.
> 90 31 7f
+ 100
! console xt 1
< b0 30 11
